# False positives: PEM header/footer MARKER STRINGS, not key material.
#
# Both connectors implement a _normalize_pem() helper that reflows a pasted
# cert/key block to strict 64-column PEM. To do that it has to know the
# header/footer delimiters, so it carries a literal list of them
# (PEM_BLOCK_TYPES in the SDK app, block_types in the classic connector):
#
#     ("-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----", "-----END CERTIFICATE-----"),
#     ("-----BEGIN PRIVATE KEY-----", "-----END PRIVATE KEY-----"),
#     ...
#
# gitleaks' private-key rule is a literal string match with no code-semantics
# awareness, so it fires on the delimiters themselves. No actual key bytes are
# present anywhere in this package: verified 2026-08-27 by reading both
# surrounding functions, and by scanning the whole export for base64 runs
# longer than 60 chars (zero hits outside the bundled wheels).
#
# Same pattern as cyberark_ccp's _normalize_pem() in the UC1 handover.
#
# NOTE: these fingerprints are line-pinned, and they HAVE drifted every time a
# connector changed: the classic connector's markers moved 402 -> 490-492
# (v1.0.6) -> 582-584 (v1.0.1, after the WHERE/limit fix and the comment
# sweep). The SDK app's have held at 128-130. Re-check both whenever either
# connector changes, or the gate will miss a real finding or fail the commit.
